{"lines":[{"x":0.8391205153558271,"t":"Reading","c":1,"w":0.072761561075846304,"y":0.11269524457478441,"h":0.013500045129351435},{"x":0.18106996000072342,"y":0.15400471132805305,"t":"READING PASSAGE 3","h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"w":0.26954732259114589},{"y":0.18444175787622474,"w":0.72232365926106779,"h":0.018665978147508921,"c":1,"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 27-40, which are based on Reading","x":0.18102452640042316},{"x":0.18106995972325615,"h":0.014567411690072807,"y":0.20200235586757143,"c":1,"w":0.1460905329386393,"t":"Passage 3 below."},{"t":"Motivational factors and the hospitality industry","y":0.23546511609668164,"h":0.017479524735988794,"w":0.52674896240234381,"x":0.28189300890412955,"c":1},{"c":1,"x":0.18106995026203529,"t":"A critical ingredient in the success of hotels is developing and maintaining superior performance","y":0.26884570090025606,"w":0.72222223917643225,"h":0.016038020171040834},{"y":0.28343023238945475,"w":0.70987655639648439,"h":0.017512052443900861,"t":"from their employees. How is that accomplished? What Human Resource Management (HRM)","c":1,"x":0.17901233868686972},{"h":0.01598837238037687,"w":0.5864197285970052,"y":0.29941860449653501,"t":"practices should organizations invest in to acquire and retain great employees?","c":1,"x":0.17901235811679708},{"w":0.720320790608724,"c":1,"y":0.3293685813846321,"x":0.18099618516016316,"h":0.017221766450520204,"t":"Some hotels aim to provide superior working conditions for their employees. The idea originated"},{"x":0.18106997885551285,"w":0.68930038452148445,"c":1,"y":0.34447674443539089,"t":"from workplaces - usually in the non-service sector - that emphasized fun and enjoyment as","h":0.014534882858869391},{"x":0.18100160750369582,"h":0.017240201345742556,"w":0.67297876993815109,"t":"part of work-life balance. By contrast, the service sector, and more specifically hotels, has","y":0.36005599884178396,"c":1},{"y":0.37632508818011701,"h":0.014723203769140158,"c":1,"x":0.18106996879514639,"t":"traditionally not extended these practices to address basic employee needs, such as good","w":0.65637858072916666},{"c":1,"x":0.18106995881440155,"t":"working conditions.","h":0.01453488398216074,"y":0.39389534869079523,"w":0.15226337432861328},{"w":0.62551442464192708,"t":"Pfeffer (1994) emphasizes that in order to succeed in a global business environment,","x":0.18312756123116003,"y":0.42285041239085697,"h":0.013250883392226021,"c":1},{"h":0.014927459689837885,"c":1,"w":0.68941304524739588,"y":0.43717770625116315,"t":"organizations must make investment in Human Resource Management (HRM) to allow them","x":0.1830705248800685},{"h":0.017986688512795279,"c":1,"y":0.45229568439440282,"t":"to acquire employees who possess better skills and capabilities than their competitors. This","x":0.17892256563830908,"w":0.67918889363606771},{"t":"investment will be to their competitive advantage. Despite this recognition of the importance","x":0.18106994680095226,"w":0.68930043538411467,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132,"y":0.46937573602737093},{"y":0.48382255511860994,"h":0.017155388920832348,"w":0.63798624674479165,"c":1,"t":"of employee development, the hospitality industry has historically been dominated by","x":0.1789513249180438},{"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"x":0.17901234102906291,"y":0.5014534882366648,"t":"underdeveloped HR practices (Lucas, 2002).","w":0.33539095560709631},{"w":0.69341562906901044,"h":0.01453488398216074,"c":1,"t":"Lucas also points out that 'the substance of HRM practices does not appear to be designed to","y":0.53052325567898651,"x":0.18106996323279967},{"t":"foster constructive relations with employees or to represent a managerial approach that enables","c":1,"y":0.54500531228354709,"x":0.18103254925565732,"w":0.70584732055664068,"h":0.015803304521720074},{"x":0.17896925826600296,"y":0.56099431622220808,"w":0.71408762613932286,"h":0.016923928569708258,"t":"developing and drawing out the full potential of people, even though employees may be broadly","c":1},{"t":"satisfied with many aspects of their work' (Lucas, 2002). In addition, or maybe as a result, high","x":0.17895246877066057,"h":0.017601344554528109,"w":0.71000890096028657,"c":1,"y":0.5759063331083798},{"t":"employee turnover has been a recurring problem throughout the hospitality industry. Among","w":0.68951161702473973,"x":0.17890912859408131,"h":0.019214385249448962,"y":0.59092058766568034,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"the many cited reasons are low compensation, inadequate benefits, poor working conditions and","w":0.71416412353515624,"y":0.60599093291308159,"h":0.017564125420488352,"x":0.18099574495363566},{"x":0.17901235092722062,"w":0.52057612101236983,"h":0.016029460129664774,"c":1,"y":0.62354651148044138,"t":"compromised employee morale and attitudes (Maroudas et al., 2008)."},{"y":0.65400471133145355,"t":"Ng and Sorensen (2008) demonstrated that when managers provide recognition to employees,","c":1,"h":0.014723203769140158,"w":0.69753087361653654,"x":0.18106995402877932},{"c":1,"w":0.69958847045898431,"y":0.66860465100681521,"x":0.17901234936056803,"h":0.016024324441826665,"t":"motivate employees to work together, and remove obstacles preventing effective performance,"},{"c":1,"y":0.68405899312536678,"x":0.1810143701256994,"h":0.015988216242885711,"w":0.68943328857421859,"t":"employees feel more obligated to stay with the company. This was succinctly summarized by"},{"t":"Michel et al. (2013): '[P]roviding support to employees gives them the confidence to perform","c":1,"x":0.18100439073114027,"w":0.69560612996419269,"h":0.01798449753310849,"y":0.69900736210969872},{"t":"their jobs better and the motivation to stay with the organization?' Hospitality organizations can","x":0.17894987061414233,"y":0.71305000746364011,"c":1,"w":0.70999893188476559,"h":0.018184744988790857},{"x":0.18106995027367437,"y":0.73110465104325495,"w":0.72222223917643236,"h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"t":"therefore enhance employee motivation and retention through the development and improvement"},{"w":0.71193415323893228,"t":"of their working conditions. These conditions are inherently linked to the working environment.","x":0.18106996030594863,"y":0.7470553591787269,"c":1,"h":0.013250883392226132},{"t":"While it seems likely that employees' reactions to their job characteristics could be affected","x":0.18095929157759941,"y":0.77394914548664029,"c":1,"w":0.67721405029296877,"h":0.019543362450122337},{"x":0.1810204057067181,"h":0.016338462964384792,"c":1,"t":"by a predisposition to view their work environment negatively, no evidence exists to support","y":0.79166672128571114,"w":0.68529724121093738},{"x":0.17894681676222471,"h":0.018717252463979928,"y":0.80643690518461442,"w":0.68945276896158858,"c":1,"t":"this hypothesis (Spector et al., 2000). However, given the opportunity, many people will find"},{"t":"25","h":0.013081395583944722,"c":1,"w":0.024691357612609877,"y":0.8677325579493067,"x":0.88477366266603175}],"h":3395,"w":2400}